  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Extended stretch of dry weather with minor wind \nimpacts from the strong coastal low this weekend\n\nA much needed break from the rain (following one of the wettest\nmid to late summer patterns on record) is expected over the \nnext 7 days across the majority of central PA. \n\nA strong coastal low developing offshore NJ/Long Island/southern\nNew England could bring some light rain to the eastern third of\nthe CWA (mainly east of US-15) later this weekend, but the main\nsensible weather impact from this system will be from the wind.\nBreezy conditions are expected Saturday and Sunday with max \ngusts 30-35 mph range over the higher terrain in the northeast \nportion of the forecast area. \n\nAs the stacked coastal low moves toward the Canadian Maritimes,\ntemperatures are projected to rebound and climb several degrees\nabove the historical average heading into the end of the month.",
